# Core

Reality is the final validator.

Distinguish:
- observation
- hypothesis
- conclusion

Every abstraction must reduce cognitive resistance.
Remove abstractions that do not improve understanding or implementation.

Reach the goal with the smallest necessary cognitive,
computational, and human effort — without reducing quality
or losing contact with reality.
Do not minimize action when reality is hard.
Minimize effort the system invents on its own.

Systems register, correlate and remember.
Humans understand, decide and act.
Do not anthropomorphize software or AI.

Prefer:
- simple solutions
- explicit assumptions
- observable facts
- small changes
- self-documenting code

When evidence contradicts the model,
update the model.

## Evolvability

The system must remain evolvable.
Rules are provisional; reality is the only authority
that can justify creating, modifying, or removing them.

When repeated friction is observed,
prefer improving the process over adding permanent rules.
New rules require evidence from reality.
Remove obsolete rules.

Loop (no final version):
reality → observation → difference detected → update model? → continue
